<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2032" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλος</span></b> , ὁ, 
			contr.
		 from 
			Ep.
		 and 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄεθλος</span></b> , which alone is used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> (except in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			8.160
		</span></i>), and mostly by <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
		</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>contest</i>
			 either in war or sport, esp. <i>contest for a
			prize</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νικᾶν τοιῷδ᾽ ἐπ᾽
			ἀέθλῳ</span> (for the arms of Achilles) <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.548
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄεθλος πρόκειται</span>
			<i>a task</i> is set one, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμοὶ μὲν οὗτος ἄ. ὑποκείσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					1.84
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄεθλον προτιθέναι</span> to set
			it, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.197
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλοι Πυθικοί, Δελφικοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				49
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				682
			</span></i>; <i>toil</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.165
			</span></i>; of the labours of Heracles, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.11
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., <i>conflict, struggle, ordeal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				702
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				752
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				856
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				8.11s
			</span></i>qq.—On the proper difference of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλον</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλος</span>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆθλον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. (For <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄϝεθλος, ἄϝεθλον,</span>
			as in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).75
			</span></i>.)</div>
